+- Images hold less memory. A decoded image's CPU pixels are dropped once a window's atlas has copied them (an image from a file, a URL or encoded bytes decodes again if it is drawn after its atlas copy was freed). Atlas pages are made at full size on the GPU only after the first upload, new pixels go up as regions, and a page no element drew from for 5 s, or the least recently drawn one while over the budget (`set_image_budget`, 64 MB of shelf pages and 128 MB in all by default), is freed with its texture. `ImageCache::decode_when_drawn` reads only an image's header until it is drawn or `Pixels::prefetch`ed; `ImageCache::file_fit` and `load_fit` decode to the box an image is drawn in (`Fit::Cover`, `Fit::Contain`); `set_max_decode_pixels` refuses larger images from their header. `Pixels::is_ready` says whether a draw shows it this frame. `image_memory` reports what images hold. Region uploads stage in 1 MiB slices. Three image decoder threads instead of four.
