+//! `El::pixels`. Each runtime keeps an RGBA atlas the renderer uploads, allocated only once an
+//! element shows pixels.
+//!
+//! Memory: a decoded image's pixels live on the CPU only until an atlas has copied them for
+//! upload. An image an [`ImageCache`](crate::ImageCache) can decode again (from a file, a URL or
+//! encoded bytes) then drops them, and the atlas keeps the GPU copy. Atlas pages are freed when
+//! no element drew from them for a while ([`IDLE_FREE`]) or when the atlas is over its budget
